# Code owners for the high-risk areas (external audit 35-08).
#
# GitHub requests a review from these owners on any PR that touches a listed
# path. Code-owner approval is required for merges to main by a separate
# ruleset (main-code-owner-review) with a repository-admin bypass for pull
# requests only: the owner authors PRs with their own account and GitHub never
# counts an author's own approval, while a non-admin collaborator with write
# access cannot merge to main (which deploys staging) without the owner's
# review. The CI checks stay required for everyone (ruleset main-protection,
# no bypass).
#
# Later patterns win, so the catch-all comes first.

